  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Issue:\navatars with massively oversized bounds will \"lock out\" the menu for quest (and pc) users and prevent them from switching with motion controllers, but, quest does not have the fallback ctrl+\\ shortcut to \"break out\". \nReplication:\nenter into an avatar with massive bounds and attempt to switch out. \n\nPossible quick resolution:\nMaking the safe mode shortcut (Both Triggers + Both Menu Buttons) change the user's local avatar to the robot as well as everyone else's would be a great workaround for these kinds of issues before the menu's selection issue can be corrected.",
